tools/__pycache__/
# recall.sh writes a usage counter beside itself, keyed on its own VAULT. Since
# 2026-09-12 a run from THIS repo is refused outright (no wiki/log.md here, so
# the history floor exits 2) — but the counter is written before that gate, so a
# refused run still drops this file. The Hub vault has ignored it since it was
# added; mirroring that decision rather than inventing a second one.
tools/.recall-counter.tsv
# NotebookLM refresh state is per-vault (it records one person's notebook IDs and
# source IDs). A refresh run from this repo drops one here; it must never be
# published from the public canonical.
tools/.notebooklm-*-state.json
